1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,325
Turn the cup over —
the water stays in?

2
00:00:04,375 --> 00:00:06,395
Fill a cup with water
right to the brim

3
00:00:06,445 --> 00:00:08,545
Cover it with thick paper
and press with your palm

4
00:00:08,595 --> 00:00:10,695
Turn it over,
then gently let go

5
00:00:10,745 --> 00:00:14,265
Always over a sink,
with an unbreakable cup!

6
00:00:14,315 --> 00:00:16,265
Fill it up!

7
00:00:16,315 --> 00:00:18,265
Paper on top, press down

8
00:00:18,315 --> 00:00:20,265
Now flip it over!

9
00:00:20,315 --> 00:00:25,035
Count to three, then gently let go

10
00:00:25,085 --> 00:00:28,805
The paper sticks
and the water stays in!

11
00:00:28,855 --> 00:00:31,005
The air around us
pushes from every direction

12
00:00:31,055 --> 00:00:33,175
The water's weight
pulls the paper down

13
00:00:33,225 --> 00:00:35,145
The air pushes the paper
up from below

14
00:00:35,195 --> 00:00:37,465
The air's push is much stronger
than the water's weight!

15
00:00:37,515 --> 00:00:41,035
The wet paper seals the gap,
so no air can get inside

16
00:00:41,085 --> 00:00:44,805
Same reason water stays in a straw
when you cover the top with your finger!

17
00:00:44,855 --> 00:00:47,255
Try it over the sink!

18
00:00:47,305 --> 00:00:49,955
Pepper on water —
why does it run away?
